      "text": "To evaluate \\(\\log_3 (27\\sqrt{3})\\), we start by expressing \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) in terms of powers of 3. We know that:\n\n\\[27 = 3^3\\]\n\\[\\sqrt{3} = 3^{1/2}\\]\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) as:\n\n\\[27\\sqrt{3} = 3^3 \\cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(\\log_3 (3^{7/2})\\). Using the property of logarithms that \\(\\log_b (b^x) = x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\\log_3 (3^{7/2}) = \\frac{7}{2}\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\log_3 (27\\sqrt{3})\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}\\).",
